How to record adapted or third-party material
--------------------------------------------
When an example crate (or documentation page) is adapted from a named public
source, contributors must record it in all three places so redistributors can
meet attribution requirements:

1. `examples/<crate>/README.md` — add an "Origin" section naming the upstream
   project, its URL, the revision or version used, the source license, and a
   short summary of what was changed. Only record sources maintainers can
   verify; do not guess at an upstream.
2. `examples/ORIGIN.md` — update the crate's row from `unreviewed` to
   `adapted` with the source link, or to `original` when the work was written
   for this repository.
3. This NOTICE file — add one row per adapted work in the table below,
   preserving any copyright or attribution text the source license requires.

For adapted material, verify the source license permits the contribution
before opening a pull request, and retain any required upstream copyright or
license notices in the crate. Flag uncertain compatibility for maintainers.

